                <pb facs="0072" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1110 Wallace, Henry A./83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-15T20:00:00-04:00">March 15, 1943—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>311. Your 348, March 12, 9 p.m. The Vice President states flatly that if any such
                    arrangements are being made they are without his knowledge or consent since he
                    does not intend to see Haya de la Torre.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
